From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:05:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Don't make the DSI line longer than the pipe
 line on VLV/CHV

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream until tested.

set_dsi_timings() converts hfp, hsync and hbp to byte clocks one by
one, each rounded up. When htotal * bpp / (8 * lanes) is not an
integer, the DSI line becomes longer than the pipe line. On a GPD Win 1
(CHV, 720x1280, htotal 774, RGB888, 4 lanes, non-burst with sync
events) each 18 px segment is 13.5 byte clocks and is programmed as 14,
so a DSI line takes 540 + 3 * 14 = 582 byte clocks while the pipe
produces a line in 580.5.

The hardware evidently honors this: the measured frame period (from the
pipe frame counter and scanline in the i915 tracepoints over 271 s) is
16.6094 ms, which is 1308 lines of 582 byte clocks at 45.833 MHz
(16.6093 ms), not the 16.5664 ms of the pipe's 61.111 MHz pixel clock.
So the DSI link paces the pipe and holds it back by 1.5 byte clocks per
line. Twice in five minutes the pipe then stalled for exactly one frame,
each time with a visible flash and MIPI_INTR_STAT DPI_FIFO_UNDERRUN
latched.

Compute the line positions in byte clocks and round them down, so the
segments add up to at most the pipe line: 540 + 13 + 14 + 13 = 580.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 877eab7..08ad31b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -1241,12 +1241,32 @@ static void set_dsi_timings(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	vbp = adjusted_mode->crtc_vtotal - adjusted_mode->crtc_vsync_end;
 
 	/* horizontal values are in terms of high speed byte clock */
-	hactive = txbyteclkhs(hactive, bpp, lane_count,
-			      intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
-	hfp = txbyteclkhs(hfp, bpp, lane_count, intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
-	hsync = txbyteclkhs(hsync, bpp, lane_count,
-			    intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
-	hbp = txbyteclkhs(hbp, bpp, lane_count, intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
+	if (!intel_dsi->dual_link && intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio == 100 &&
+	    (display->platform.valleyview || display->platform.cherryview)) {
+		/*
+		 * EXPERIMENT: round the line positions (not each segment) down,
+		 * so the DSI line is never longer than the pipe line. Rounding
+		 * each of hfp/hsync/hbp up makes the link line longer than the
+		 * pipe line when htotal * bpp / (8 * lanes) is not an integer.
+		 */
+		u32 hs = adjusted_mode->crtc_hsync_start * bpp / (8 * lane_count);
+		u32 he = adjusted_mode->crtc_hsync_end * bpp / (8 * lane_count);
+		u32 ht = adjusted_mode->crtc_htotal * bpp / (8 * lane_count);
+		u32 ha = adjusted_mode->crtc_hdisplay * bpp / (8 * lane_count);
+
+		hactive = txbyteclkhs(hactive, bpp, lane_count,
+				      intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
+		hfp = hs - ha;
+		hsync = he - hs;
+		hbp = ht - he;
+	} else {
+		hactive = txbyteclkhs(hactive, bpp, lane_count,
+				      intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
+		hfp = txbyteclkhs(hfp, bpp, lane_count, intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
+		hsync = txbyteclkhs(hsync, bpp, lane_count,
+				    intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
+		hbp = txbyteclkhs(hbp, bpp, lane_count, intel_dsi->burst_mode_ratio);
+	}
 
 	for_each_dsi_port(port, intel_dsi->ports) {
 		if (display->platform.geminilake || display->platform.broxton) {
-- 
